# Owner Event Binding Rules

## 1. Direct native binding

- Critical operator actions (Drop Curtain, go-live, end broadcast) MUST attach `onClick={handler}` directly on the native `<button type="button">` element.
- Do not wrap these controls in intermediate client components solely to host click logic unless the wrapper adds no extra DOM layers.
- Parent layout containers (`section`, `article`, `div`) MUST NOT register `onClick`, `onPointerDown`, or `pointer-events-none` that block child buttons.

## 2. No silent failures under pressure

- Drop Curtain and other emergency controls MUST call `window.alert()` when the API returns a non-200 response or the fetch throws, in addition to inline UI status text.
- Handlers live in the workspace client (`OwnerControlClient`) and are passed as props into presentational wizards.

## 3. Presentational wizards

- `BroadcastControlWizard` and sibling room shells are presentational — they receive `onDropCurtain`, `onGoLive`, etc. from the client workspace and bind them without indirection or default no-op swallowing in production paths.
